```apex
public with sharing class AccountCountrySync {

    /**
     * When an Account's BillingCountry changes, propagate the new value to the
     * MailingCountry of that Account's Contacts whose MailingCountry is blank or
     * equal to the Account's previous BillingCountry. Contacts with any other
     * MailingCountry (working abroad) are left alone.
     */
    public static void syncContactCountries(
        Map<Id, Account> oldMap,
        Map<Id, Account> newMap
    ) {
        // 1. Identify accounts whose BillingCountry actually changed.
        //    Store old/new country per account so we know how to decide later.
        Map<Id, String> oldCountryByAccount = new Map<Id, String>();
        Map<Id, String> newCountryByAccount = new Map<Id, String>();

        for (Account newAcc : newMap.values()) {
            Account oldAcc = oldMap.get(newAcc.Id);
            String oldCountry = oldAcc.BillingCountry;
            String newCountry = newAcc.BillingCountry;

            if (!equalsNullSafe(oldCountry, newCountry)) {
                oldCountryByAccount.put(newAcc.Id, oldCountry);
                newCountryByAccount.put(newAcc.Id, newCountry);
            }
        }

        // Nothing changed: bail out before spending a query.
        if (oldCountryByAccount.isEmpty()) {
            return;
        }

        Set<Id> changedAccountIds = oldCountryByAccount.keySet();

        // 2. One query, filtered to only the affected accounts.
        //    (A blanket "SELECT ... FROM Contact" would blow the 50,000-row
        //     query limit on an org with millions of contacts.)
        List<Contact> contactsToUpdate = new List<Contact>();

        for (Contact con : [
            SELECT Id, AccountId, MailingCountry
            FROM Contact
            WHERE AccountId IN :changedAccountIds
        ]) {
            String prevCountry = oldCountryByAccount.get(con.AccountId);
            String newCountry  = newCountryByAccount.get(con.AccountId);

            Boolean isBlank      = String.isBlank(con.MailingCountry);
            Boolean matchedOldHq = equalsNullSafe(con.MailingCountry, prevCountry);

            if (isBlank || matchedOldHq) {
                con.MailingCountry = newCountry;
                contactsToUpdate.add(con);
            }
        }

        // 3. Single DML.
        if (!contactsToUpdate.isEmpty()) {
            update contactsToUpdate;
        }
    }

    private static Boolean equalsNullSafe(String a, String b) {
        if (a == null && b == null) {
            return true;
        }
        if (a == null || b == null) {
            return false;
        }
        return a.equals(b);
    }
}
```

**Notes on the decisions:**

- **Filtered query instead of full-table scan.** The only change from your plan; explained above. This is the difference between code that works and code that throws every run.
- **`equalsNullSafe` for the change check.** `BillingCountry` can be `null` on either side; comparing `null` values correctly avoids false "changed" detections and keeps the trigger from doing needless work.
- **Blank handling via `String.isBlank`.** Treats `null` and `''` as blank, which matches "blank or equal to the previous country."
- **Early exit** when no account's country changed — saves the query entirely for unrelated account updates.
- **Bulk-safe:** at most one SOQL and one DML regardless of batch size (200 accounts → one query scoped to those accounts).

