The key challenge: NPSP's household logic. When you insert a Contact with no AccountId, NPSP auto-creates a Household Account for each contact individually. To get ONE household for all members, I need to create the household account first, assign all contacts to it, then set the primary contact.

To avoid leaving extra/empty households behind, I create the household account explicitly with the HH_Account record type, insert the contacts with that AccountId set (so NPSP doesn't create new households), then set the primary contact reference.

