public with sharing class ContactImportService {
    /**
     * Inserts the given contacts in a single DML statement while skipping the
     * TA_Contact_CreateWelcomeTask action (so migrated existing customers do
     * not receive a welcome task). All other Contact automation still runs,
     * including TA_Contact_FormatPhone.
     *
     * The action-level bypass is restored to its prior state before returning,
     * so contacts inserted later in the same transaction behave normally.
     */
    public static void importContacts(List<Contact> contacts) {
        if (contacts == null || contacts.isEmpty()) {
            return;
        }

        // Remember whether the action was already bypassed so we don't clobber
        // an existing bypass set elsewhere in this transaction.
        Boolean wasAlreadyBypassed =
            MetadataTriggerHandler.isBypassed(TA_Contact_CreateWelcomeTask.class);

        if (!wasAlreadyBypassed) {
            MetadataTriggerHandler.bypass(TA_Contact_CreateWelcomeTask.class);
        }

        try {
            insert contacts;
        } finally {
            if (!wasAlreadyBypassed) {
                MetadataTriggerHandler.clearBypass(TA_Contact_CreateWelcomeTask.class);
            }
        }
    }
}
```

The key is to bypass the Account sObject for the whole transaction scope, do both DMLs, and restore in a `finally` block. I must preserve prior bypass state so that "normal" behavior resumes correctly (if something else had already bypassed Account, I shouldn't blindly clear it — but the spec says Account automation must behave normally after, so restoring to prior state is the correct interpretation).

